{:kind :masorah, :count 12, :occurrences ["נשיא"]} {:kind :other, :note "Six verses per prince × twelve princes, each name doubled = 24 corresponding to 24 hours"} {:kind :gematria, :a "שלשים ומאה", :b "שנות אדם עד שנולד שת"}], :frame {:text "The tribe of Judah humbled itself: Judah said to Joseph 'Let your servant remain instead of the lad' (Genesis 44:33), and David is called 'he is the smallest' (1 Samuel 17:14). Six things were renewed on the day the Tabernacle was dedicated (Sotah 37a; Megillah 10b): the Shekhinah rested, the princes brought offerings, the priestly blessing was given, the camp was arranged, bamot were prohibited, and fire descended. Nahshon leapt first into the Sea of Reeds before it split (Sotah 37a). The founding verses for David's qualities are 1 Samuel 16:18; for the Messiah, Isaiah 11:2; for Daniel and companions, Daniel 1:4. Adam begot Seth at 130 years (Genesis 5:3).", :sources ["Genesis 44:33" "1 Samuel 17:14" "1 Samuel 16:18" "Isaiah 11:2" "Daniel 1:4" "Genesis 5:3" "Sotah 37a" "Megillah 10b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שבעים שקל", :translit "shiv'im shekel", :gloss "seventy shekels"} {:he "שבעים", :translit "shiv'im", :gloss "seventy"} {:he "שבעים אומות", :translit "shiv'im umot", :gloss "seventy nations"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Seventy shekels correspond to seventy years left to his sons and deliverance from seventy nations"}], :frame {:text "Seventy nations descend from Noah's sons, listed in the Table of Nations (Genesis 10). The number seventy is associated with completeness of the gentile world.", :sources ["Genesis 10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שבעים שקל", :translit "shiv'im shekel", :gloss "seventy shekels"} {:he "שבעים נפש", :translit "shiv'im nefesh", :gloss "seventy souls"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "שבעים שקל", :b "שבעים נפש"}], :frame {:text "Seventy souls of Israel went down to Egypt: 'All the persons of the house of Jacob who came to Egypt were seventy' (Genesis 46:27).", :sources ["Genesis 46:27"]}}], :arithmeti